Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch — no real network calls. Covers constructor validation, fetch request construction, response parsing, error handling, and mock mode behavior.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts contains at least 5 vitest tests with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach fetch restoration, covering: (a) correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, (b) successful response parsed into FlightResult[], (c) HTTP 4xx rejection with status code in error message, (d) missing/empty API key constructor error, (e) malformed/missing-fields response body rejects with parse/validation error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture without invoking fetch — spy on global fetch and assert it was never called
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API unset, empty string, or non-'true' values (e.g. 'false', '1', 'TRUE') result in a real fetch call — mock mode is strict opt-in, not a fuzzy truthy check
- Test verifies real HTTP/API failures (4xx, 5xx, network error, malformed body) are never silently replaced with mock/fixture data
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class name is SkyscannerClient, exported as default from module
- Constructor signature: constructor(options: SkyscannerClientOptions = {}) where options has optional apiKey?: string
- Constructor error message: 'Missing RapidAPI key: provide apiKey in constructor or set RAPIDAPI_KEY env var'
- Constructor resolves apiKey precedence: constructor-provided apiKey > RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- Constructor accepts empty string apiKey as falsy — triggers missing key error
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- Mock mode is enabled ONLY when process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict string equality, case-sensitive)
- Mock mode returns deterministic fixtures from getMockResults(params) without calling fetch
- Mock mode fixture prices are: 199.5, 312.75, 540.0 (all USD currency)
- Real API endpoint: https://skyscanner-skyscanner-flight-search-v1.p.rapidapi.com/apiservices/browseroutes/v1.0/US/USD/en-US/{origin}/{destination}/{date}
- Request headers: 'X-RapidAPI-Key', 'X-RapidAPI-Host', 'Accept: application/json'
- Network errors throw with message prefix: 'Skyscanner network error: ' + original message
- HTTP non-ok responses throw with message: 'Skyscanner API error: HTTP ' + status + ' ' + statusText
- Parse errors throw with message prefix: 'Skyscanner parse error: ' + original message
- parseFlightResults validates all 7 required fields on each candidate: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- parseFlightResults accepts body as array OR object with Quotes array property
- Empty results throw: 'Malformed Skyscanner response: no flight results found'
- Missing field errors throw with pattern: 'Malformed Skyscanner response: missing {field} field'
- Non-object candidate throws: 'Malformed Skyscanner response: flight entry is not an object'
- No validation on adults parameter — adults=0, adults=-1, adults=undefined all accepted
- No validation on origin/destination/date format — any string accepted
- No retry logic exists for failed requests
- No timeout configuration exists on fetch call

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

